# Persist the clock every five minutes.
#
# With no RTC the saved timestamp is the only thing standing between a reset
# and a boot back at the epoch, and resets are how this board is driven all
# day. Five minutes bounds how stale the restored clock can be; the write is
# twenty bytes to the card. (It was hourly, into a tmpfs path, so it saved
# nothing - see S30clock.)
*/5 * * * * /etc/init.d/S30clock save
